# Docker & Containers Prerequisite for Kubernetes

> Based on the Kubernetes learning approach recommended by TechWorld with Nana.
>
> Goal: Build a solid foundation in Docker and Containers before learning Kubernetes.

---

# Phase 1: Understand Why Containers Exist

## Problem with Traditional Deployment

Imagine a Java application:

```text
Application
├── Java 17
├── Maven
├── Spring Boot
└── Linux Dependencies
```

### Problems

- Works on your laptop
- Fails on QA server
- Different Java versions
- Different OS libraries

Example:

```bash
Error:
Java version mismatch
```

### Solution: Containers

A container packages everything the application needs.

```text
Container
├── Application
├── Java Runtime
├── Libraries
└── Configurations
```

Benefits:

- Consistent deployment
- Portable across environments
- Faster startup
- Better resource utilization

