# Phase 11: Docker Volumes

## Problem

Container data is lost when the container is removed.

Example:

```bash
docker rm mysql
```

All database data disappears.

---

## Create Volume

```bash
docker volume create mysql-data
```

View volumes:

```bash
docker volume ls
```

Run MySQL using volume:

```bash
docker run -d \
-v mysql-data:/var/lib/mysql \
mysql
```

Now the data survives container deletion.

### Kubernetes Mapping

```text
Docker Volume
        ↓
Persistent Volume (PV)
Persistent Volume Claim (PVC)
```

---

# Phase 12: Docker Networking

Create network:

```bash
docker network create my-network
```

Check networks:

```bash
docker network ls
```

Run MySQL:

```bash
docker run -d \
--network my-network \
--name mysql \
mysql
```

Run backend:

```bash
docker run -d \
--network my-network \
--name backend \
backend-app
```

Backend connects to MySQL using:

```text
mysql:3306
```

Docker automatically creates DNS records.

### Kubernetes Mapping

```text
Docker Network
        ↓
Kubernetes Networking
        ↓
Services + DNS
```

